ng very many  thing  was happening the idea  and the kind of understanding of this  being an explosion caused by  material that was stored in the port had  become i think  a lot more prevalent and there was real  anger and resentment and frustration  growing in building  at that reality  these protests firstly have been going  on now  for three days saturday the city erupted  convulsing with fury  at a government which has allowed  thousands of tons of ammonium nitrate to  be negligently stored  in terms of the cause of this blast this  may have been  explosive material that was being held  confiscated material  that may have ignited and caused this  explosion but that the security forces  are still  investigating i have to say after two  weeks  on the 18th of august i have received  the only call from an official asking me  to come to rafael hariri  hospital because the dna  my dna match was a body dna  and it was confirmed that it was my  father's  body we've waited 14 days  to know the destiny of my father they  didn't care  to have such an explosive material  located unprotected  in this place they weren't considering  the human fact  about governing a country  my father was our rock so  he would like be there always whenever  wherever  he wanted to spend as much time as he  can with me  he wanted me to prove myself before  getting married  he always believed in my capacities  and in me being a strong independent  woman  we start with breaking news this  afternoon from lebanon where the prime  minister hassan  diab is expected to stand down shortly  the rest of his government has already  resigned following mounting anger in the  country  over the devastating explosion in favor  of this good lifespan  ali and tatiana the hasruti family  are amongst many hundreds of families in  lebanon who to this day  refuse to give up and refuse to back  down in the demands for justice  they feel that it's their right and it  is their right to  to know why their loved ones were taken  away from them  in such a horrific manner  justice is my vision is my mission to do  [Music]  i cannot accept that another young girl  would be deprived of her father of his  affection and of his love  because of their corruption and  selfishness i cannot accept that  and i'm gonna work as  as hard as i can to ensure that justice  is going to be served  lebanon as a country was already  struggling so much  before the events of august the 4th  before that explosion  but the explosion really tipped it over  because what happened after the beirut  blast  i think changed people's lives forever  for that explosion to have happened  in the center of a capital city with so  many  normal ordinary innocent people trying  to just live their lives as best as they  can  in the grips of a crisis for that to  have happened  i think took that sense of  protection or that sense of security  away  and what it's left actually is a country  in  almost constant mourning is an economy  that has been totally shattered  it's people bereft and unable to survive  because they've lost  loved ones because they've lost their  support system because they've lost  their homes and their livelihoods  they've lost their jobs  you consider the amount of destruction  you consider  more than 200 people killed thousands  injured billions of pounds worth of  damage done  just how so many months afterwards there  still hasn't been  serious accountability and justice is  just unfathomable it was  one of my greatest fear to lose my  father because we are a  very close family and  what i said in his family  that loved or don't die and  we've experienced love with her and  this love will be born in us and  way bigger and i'm better  as a trend in history that  everything will get better and  we're going to a world with more justice  less  less harder  as of august 2021 the number of recorded  deaths from the beirut explosion  stands at 211 with more than 6 000  injured justice campaigners say  authorities continue to obstruct their  efforts to bring about a proper  investigation into the disaster the  beirut blast  kazan's story was written and produced  by rob mulhern  with zane jafar for more information log  on to skynews.com  forward slash storycast 21  storycast 21 will now take a break for  august  the series resumes in september starting  with an extended episode  to mark the 20th anniversary of the 9 11  attacks  i arrived in new york suitcase under one  arm  dog under the other arm i couldn't  believe that not only was i working  there but i was working in the world  trade center  head office was on the 84th floor of two  world trade center  which was the south tower

